  "routing_constraints": [
    "F high-current primary paths: VBUS into high-side drain; high-side SOURCE to low-side drain PHASE; low-side SOURCE to RS pad1; RS pad2 to DC- GND. Parallel wide copper/planes must preserve these same nets.",
    "Each B PHASE region is nominally x44..59,yphase-2..yphase+5. Form a real broad corridor from high-source vias through low-drain vias to J4; do not let a gate, input, bootstrap or sample trace cut its only main-current neck.",
    "C26/C30 sit at the lower-left boundary of the PHASE field. Keep their VBOOT pads out of the main PHASE corridor; put the high-source via array nearer source pads2/3, not underneath the capacitor courtyard. C34 is on F instead.",
    "Use actual pad coordinates for the 8-pin MOSFETs. Large drain pad5 and toes5/6/7/8 are one drain net; source1/2/3 are one source net. Preserve gate4 and the original source/drain net identities.",
    "Driver COM and its VCC capacitors return to the phase-specific SOURCE on the shunt high side, never directly to global GND. SOURCE must not acquire a ground-plane or mounting-hole bypass around RS.",
    "INA U10/U11/U12 pin8 takes a separate Kelvin route from RS pad1 SOURCE, pin1 a separate Kelvin route from RS pad2 GND. Do not share a high-current stem before either Kelvin branch. The other ground pins and decoupler may join the local quiet GND.",
    "Route each HO/LO pair with its own nearby VS/SOURCE return. The driver LO pin is on the left and the low-side MOS gate is on the right; reserve a direct inner-layer paired route rather than an arbitrary perimeter detour.",
    "Keep C25/C26, C29/C30 and C33/C34 strictly between VBOOT and PHASE; bootstrap returns must not join GND or SOURCE.",
    "The two existing C21/C22 MLCCs are retained at their defined positions; use broad short VBUS/GND connections and verify the W bridge commutation loop after routing. Two shared capacitors do not guarantee local W-loop impedance.",
    "Six-layer draft follows root plan: In1/In4 quiet continuous GND, In3 right-side VBUS power copper, B local PHASE copper and remaining signal routing. Maintain sense/driver return paths when splitting power islands.",
    "J3/J4/J5 wire pads have courtyards on both faces. Their plated holes, soldered wires and strain relief are mechanical exclusions, not just an F-side component outline.",
    "Electrolytic footprints have only F courtyards; their actual pad copper plus0.25mm mechanical margin was separately excluded from B SMD courtyards. Check solder protrusion, 25mm capacitor height, screw heads and real washer dimensions during 3D/assembly review."
  ]
